      "extract": "We have reformulated the bosonic sector of Weinberg-Salam theory in terms of quaternions. It predicts mH=j2mw and sin2 Bw=1/4 at the classical level. The renormalization effects are not considered in this paper. The present experimentsl3) indicate that mHo>48 GeV, mw=80 GeV and sin 2Bw=0.23, 10 % down from 0.25. If the relation mH=j2mw is correct within ±10 % corrections, the Higgs mass would be in the range 100 ~",
